<title>SINGAPORE: Vitol wins Madras low aromatic naphtha at -$24/T.</title>
<headline>Vitol wins Madras low aromatic naphtha at -$24/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has awarded Dutch trader Vitol its sell tender for low aromatic naphtha (LAN) from Madras on the east coast at $24.00 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 27,000-tonne cargo, lifting May 27-29, was awarded on a free-on-board (fob) basis in a tender which closed May 15 and was valid for a day.</p>
<p>The award was lower than IOC's last Madras LAN award, lifting May 12-14, which was awarded to South Korean refiner Hanwha at $19.50 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes, fob.  </p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
</text>
